  "described": {
    "alt_text": "A square oil painting of pastel pink, peach, mint and lilac blocks, grid spheres and splash shapes, with small faces in windows and no blue anywhere.",
    "description": "A square oil painting on canvas. Rounded blocks and machine forms in pink, peach, mint, lilac and mustard are stacked from the lower left, with window slots, portholes and a small figure with a hooded head in a window at lower left. Grid patterned spheres, one large at left and smaller ones scattered, float among coral or splash shapes in the upper half. A curved rail or track sweeps from the left sphere down into the blocks. A small scrawl of hash marks sits at upper right. Thick black outlines and visible brushwork. The palette avoids blue entirely.",
    "impression": "A companion to Almost Blueless Spaceland, this time with the blue removed completely, so everything is warm and powdery like a pastry shop. The grid spheres are the only hard geometry in a world of soft blocks. It feels like a quiet corner of the Superland factory.",
